{"5261040":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Panorama of All Beings","steam_appid":5261040,"required_age":0,"is_free":true,"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The thoughts of all beings paint a work without an owner.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Panorama of All Beings is an online multiplayer pixel-art game. All players share one 1920 × 1080 world canvas. Choose a cell, give it a colour, and contribute to pictures built one pixel at a time.From a single pixel, you plant your own will.Or leave your mark upon the countless wills of others.Every stroke is an expression. Time will filter out the noise, and what remains in the end is the answer we all create together.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>How to play<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the canvas, select a cell and a colour, then confirm your change. After each successful placement, wait for the cooldown shown in the interface before placing another pixel. While waiting, explore other areas, read comments, or revisit the canvas history.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start your own pattern, help complete another player's picture, repair a changed section, or transform an existing design.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Collaborate—and adapt to other players<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nobody permanently owns a pixel. You can overwrite another player's colour, and other players can overwrite yours. Overwriting is part of the game: pictures can grow, change, or disappear as people contribute.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The challenge comes from choosing how to use each placement in a shared space that keeps changing. Multiplayer interaction takes place on the public canvas, without creating private rooms or waiting for a match.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Explore the canvas history<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Scrub through or play the history timeline to see how pictures appeared, developed, and were rewritten. Discover the process behind the canvas, not just its current appearance.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discuss what you discover<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use location-based comments to discuss pictures and respond to other players. Likes, reporting, and personal blocking are also available.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Before you play<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is an open-ended creative experience. Set your own drawing goals, contribute to an existing design, or simply explore the canvas and its history.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The world canvas requires an internet connection and Steam authentication. Changes are saved on the server, but your pixels can still be overwritten by other players. English and Simplified Chinese interfaces are supported.  <\/p>","about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The thoughts of all beings paint a work without an owner.<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Panorama of All Beings is an online multiplayer pixel-art game. All players share one 1920 × 1080 world canvas. Choose a cell, give it a colour, and contribute to pictures built one pixel at a time.From a single pixel, you plant your own will.Or leave your mark upon the countless wills of others.Every stroke is an expression. Time will filter out the noise, and what remains in the end is the answer we all create together.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>How to play<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore the canvas, select a cell and a colour, then confirm your change. After each successful placement, wait for the cooldown shown in the interface before placing another pixel. While waiting, explore other areas, read comments, or revisit the canvas history.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start your own pattern, help complete another player's picture, repair a changed section, or transform an existing design.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Collaborate—and adapt to other players<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Nobody permanently owns a pixel. You can overwrite another player's colour, and other players can overwrite yours. Overwriting is part of the game: pictures can grow, change, or disappear as people contribute.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The challenge comes from choosing how to use each placement in a shared space that keeps changing. Multiplayer interaction takes place on the public canvas, without creating private rooms or waiting for a match.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Explore the canvas history<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Scrub through or play the history timeline to see how pictures appeared, developed, and were rewritten. Discover the process behind the canvas, not just its current appearance.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discuss what you discover<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use location-based comments to discuss pictures and respond to other players. Likes, reporting, and personal blocking are also available.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Before you play<\/strong><\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is an open-ended creative experience. Set your own drawing goals, contribute to an existing design, or simply explore the canvas and its history.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The world canvas requires an internet connection and Steam authentication. Changes are saved on the server, but your pixels can still be overwritten by other players. English and Simplified Chinese interfaces are supported.  <\/p>","short_description":"An online multiplayer pixel-art game on one shared 1920 x 1080 canvas. Place a pixel, wait for the cooldown, then contribute again. Build on others' designs or overwrite them—and expect yours to change too. Discuss the canvas through comments and replay its history. Internet required.","supported_languages":"English, Simplified Chinese","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5261040\/e863fa6cbcb031aa1aacf0f5a4660e1cd8bb382c\/header.jpg?t=1793642452","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5261040\/5dcd544aa860f1d4c770e4623dcead2ce35d18a4\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793642452","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5261040\/5dcd544aa860f1d4c770e4623dcead2ce35d18a4\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793642452","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>Network:<\/strong> Broadband Internet connection<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> Requires a 64-bit operating system and an internet connection to access the shared canvas.<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["Haolin Zhao"],"publishers":["Haolin Zhao"],"package_groups":[],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"categories":[{"id":1,"description":"Multi-player"},{"id":9,"description":"Co-op"},{"id":38,"description":"Online Co-op"},{"id":80,"description":"#category_playable_at_your_own_pace"},{"id":74,"description":"Playable without Timed Input"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}],"genres":[{"id":"4","description":"Casual"},{"id":"23","description":"Indie"},{"id":"37","description":"Free To Play"}],"screenshots":[{"id":0,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5261040\/226551f8a2280a155aa86a39